  "prefLabel": "Pda 101.24 Mooring anchor",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pda 101.24 “Mooring anchor” means any anchor or weight which is designed to rest on the bed or to be buried in the bed of state tidal waters, attached by a chain, cable, rope or other mechanism to a mooring buoy, and left in position permanently or on a seasonal basis.\n\nSource. #8760, eff 11-18-06 (formerly Pda 101.16)",
